{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 31, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "**A Whirlwind Journey Through Japan: Cherry Blossoms and Culinary Delights**\n\nLast spring, my adventure in Japan began in Tokyo, where the neon-lit streets of Shibuya buzzed with energy. The iconic Scramble Crossing, though chaotic, felt like a dance of urban life. My first stop: a tiny sushi bar in Tsukiji, where the chefs prepared nigiri with precision. Each bite was fresh perfection.\n\nThe real magic, though, was in Kyoto. Wandering through Maruyama Park, I was stunned by the sea of sakura—cherry blossoms in full bloom—pink petals drifting like confetti. I joined locals for hanami picnics under their delicate canopies, sharing sake and onigiri as the sun dipped below the horizon.\n\nOut in the countryside, Nara’s friendly deer trotted alongside me, their bells chiming softly. The Todai-ji Temple, home to the world’s largest bronze Buddha, loomed majestically. Nearby, the serene Koyasan offered a taste of tranquility—monks chanted in the evening while I sipped matcha in a ryokan’s tatami room.\n\nMy last night was in Osaka, where a street food feast of takoyaki and okonomiyaki left me utterly satisfied. The city’s vibrancy was a perfect finale.\n\nJapan was a masterclass in contrasts—ancient and modern, frenetic and peaceful. I left with full memories, a suitcase of souvenirs, and a promise to return.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.06550939381122589}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.27843376994132996}, {"token": " Wh", "logprob": -0.037113383412361145}, {"token": "irl", "logprob": -0.018043426796793938}, {"token": "wind", "logprob": -4.7801782784517854e-05}, {"token": " Journey", "logprob": -1.7555687427520752}, {"token": " Through", "logprob": -0.007896515540778637}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -0.008402354083955288}, {"token": ":", "logprob": -2.790689468383789}, {"token": " Cherry", "logprob": -1.1284183263778687}, {"t